<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 52/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Evaluates the 3x3 Jacobian J0 and linear Turing dispersion curve sigma(k) of Nakamasu et al. (2009) across k in [0, 6.5] (L27-68), but `synthesize_cosine_stripes` (L71-79) uses a heuristic cosine wave rather than integrating the coupled 3-variable nonlinear reaction-diffusion PDE for melanophores (u), xanthophores (v), and long-range survival factor (w) with saturating production clip(a*u + b*v + d*w + e, 0, F_max), and omits both laser-ablation regeneration polarity (Figs. 2-3) and horizontal myoseptum / iridophore X0 pioneer guidance." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py L71–L79: Heuristic cosine superposition instead of nonlinear 3-species (u,v,w) reaction-diffusion PDE + laser ablation solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py#L71-L79>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-model-fidelity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
